{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1961 Verified -1: MY BUG, and a repeat of a lesson. I added rows to a SHARED fixture in tests/unit/test_audit_ticket_page_heldout.py whose test pins a '1/2' completion met-count, making it 1/4. It passed locally ONLY because the entire file SKIPS without fastapi - my '6 passed' came wholly from the other file, so I edited that file blind and never ran it. Fixed properly: installed the ui extras (fastapi, jinja2, uvicorn) into the worktree venv, reproduced the failure locally, restored the file from origin/main, and added a SEPARATE test with its own ticket and fixture asserting both kind spellings render and that lacking is [True,True,False]. 16 passed locally for real; 46 passed across the S7 suites; lint clean. Amended 1961 with --no-edit so Change-Id I1c2ccfcc and the sign-off survived. LESSON (generalises the earlier bare-pytest one): a SKIP is not a PASS - check what was skipped instead of reading the green summary."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787258674151784001,"uuid":"dceaf93b-60b6-4b5d-bfa8-f51931fc03f6"}